          "ruleId": "procfs_sysrq",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Container escape chain detected (severity=high, score=0.73).\n\nChain: /proc/sysrq-trigger abuse\n\nWriting to /proc/sysrq-trigger can crash or reboot the host kernel, causing denial of service. Requires both write access to the procfs path AND CAP_SYS_ADMIN \u2014 non-privileged containers see the file as writable per DAC but the kernel rejects the write with EROFS.",
