          "ruleId": "proc_fd_symlink_traversal",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Container escape chain detected (severity=high, score=0.71).\n\nChain: /proc/self/fd symlink to host\n\nSymlinks in /proc/self/fd can point to host filesystem locations, enabling file reads/writes outside the container. Every container has /proc/self/fd; the exploit primitive only yields host access when combined with a capability that permits reading the symlink target (CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH or CAP_SYS_ADMIN), or with CVE-2024-21626-style runc fd leaks.",
            "markdown": "### /proc/self/fd symlink to host\n\n**Severity:** high \u00b7 **Composite score:** 0.71\n\n**PoC:**\n```sh\n# Traverse /proc/self/fd symlinks to access host files\nls -la /proc/self/fd/ && readlink /proc/self/fd/*\n```"
